mips: Ingenic MXU2 128-bit SIMD unit (XBurst1 T-series)

MXU2 is the coprocessor-2 SIMD unit of the Ingenic XBurst1 T-series cores
(T10, T20, T21, T23, T30, T31): 32 x 128-bit vector registers $vr0..$vr31
and a control register MCSR ($31), reached through COP2 (major 010010) and
SPECIAL2 (major 011100) encodings.  It is the successor to the 64-bit MXU1
of earlier JZ parts; the XBurst1 core programming manual's SOC feature
table lists "Ingenic MXU2: Yes" for the T-series only, and the 3.10 kernel
enables it lazily: cpu_probe_ingenic sets MIPS_ASE_XBURSTMXUV2 when
Config1.C2 is set, and the first MXU2 instruction in a thread takes a CU2
Coprocessor-Unusable trap whose handler sets Status.CU2 and context-switches
the 32 registers with the COP2/SPECIAL2-encoded su1q/lu1q/cfcmxu/ctcmxu
instructions (arch/mips/xburst/core/mxu-v2-ex.obj).

This models MXU2 in TCG.  New files:

 * target/mips/tcg/mxu2.decode       - decodetree for the ASE
 * target/mips/tcg/mxu2_translate.c  - trans_* handlers + CU2 gating
 * target/mips/tcg/mxu2_helper.c     - run-time helpers
 * target/mips/tcg/mxu2_helper.h.inc - helper prototypes
 * target/mips/tcg/mxu2_ops.h        - op codes / element addressing

with minimal hooks: MXU2Reg[32] + MCSR added to CPUMIPSState (cleared by
reset via end_reset_fields, migrated by a vmstate subsection present only
when ASE_MXU2 is set), a MIPS_HFLAG_CU2 recomputed in compute_hflags from
Status.CU2, ASE_MXU2 in mips-defs.h, and a decode hook in decode_opc().

CU2 gating: every MXU2 instruction raises Coprocessor Unusable with CE=2
when Status.CU2=0, so the kernel's lazy enable works.  The "XBurst1" model
(patch 0015) advertises Config1.C2, ASE_MXU2 and a writable Status.CU2.

Encodings were recovered from the Ingenic GCC 5.4 toolchain's libopcodes
(the MXU2 opcode table: match/mask/operand strings), with every operand
field confirmed by assembling each form with `as -mmxu2` and reading the
resulting words; the test program checks the decode end to end.

Semantics.  Where an encoding and the GCC intrinsic (<mxu2.h>) name an
operation unambiguously and it matches an MSA operation (MXU2's mnemonics
closely follow MSA's), it is implemented with that meaning, reusing the
layout/semantics of the analogous MSA op:

 * Inline gvec (mxu2_translate.c): add/sub/mul, signed/unsigned saturating
   add/sub (ADDSS/ADDUU/SUBSS/SUBUU), smin/smax/umin/umax, vector and
   immediate shifts (SLL/SRA/SRL, SLLI/SRAI/SRLI), AND/OR/XOR/NOR and the
   byte-immediate ANDIB/ORIB/XORIB/NORIB, element compares
   CEQ/CNE/CLTS/CLTU/CLES/CLEU and compare-with-zero CEQZ/CNEZ/CLTZ/CLEZ.
 * Helper (mxu2_helper.c): MAXA/MINA, ADDA/ADDAS, SUBSA/SUBUA/SUBUS,
   AVES/AVEU/AVERS/AVERU (floor/round averaging), SRAR/SRLR/SRARI/SRLRI
   (rounding shifts), DIVS/DIVU/MODS/MODU, MADD/MSUB, widening dot products
   DOTPS/DOTPU and the accumulating DADDS/DADDU/DSUBS/DSUBU, Q15/Q31
   MULQ/MULQR/MADDQ/MADDQR/MSUBQ/MSUBQR, SATS/SATU, LOC/LZC/BCNT, the
   element permute SHUFV, and all floating point (FADD..FMINA, FCEQ/FCLT/
   FCLE/FCOR, FSQRT, FCLASS, the VCVT/VTRUNC conversions) using QEMU's
   softfloat with the active FPU rounding mode.
 * Moves/fills: LI, MFCPU (broadcast GPR), REPX/REPI (broadcast element),
   INSFCPU/INSFMXU (insert element), MTCPUS/MTCPUU (element -> GPR),
   MFFPU/MTFPU/INSFFPU (FPR <-> element), CTCMXU/CFCMXU (MCSR), BSELV.
 * Loads/stores: LU1Q/SU1Q (byte displacement), LA1Q/SA1Q (displacement
   scaled by 16) and the indexed LU1QX/SU1QX/LA1QX/SA1QX.
 * Branches: BZ/BZV (bnez/beqz per element size and the whole-register
   1q form), matching MSA BNZ/BZ and GCC's divide-guard use of bnez4w.

Best guesses, flagged "GUESS" in the code and mirrored by the test's
reference:

 * BSELV bit-select direction (mask bit 1 -> vt).
 * SHUFV control layout: index (element<<1)|from_vs, derived from the
   constant control tables a vendor binary builds for it; only byte
   granularity is seen in the wild.
 * DIVS/DIVU by zero return 0 and MODS/MODU by zero return the dividend
   (trapless; the real unit's divide-by-zero behaviour is unconfirmed, and
   GCC guards the divide intrinsics with bnez4w + break anyway).
 * VCVTH/VCVTQ/VCVTR/VCVTQE/VCVTQO narrowing / Q-format / round-variant
   conversions: implemented plausibly but not confirmed from the sources;
   none appear in the vendor binaries examined.

diff --git a/target/mips/cpu.h b/target/mips/cpu.h
index dfc1c79..cec4b6d 100644
--- a/target/mips/cpu.h
+++ b/target/mips/cpu.h
@@ -25,6 +25,19 @@ union wr_t {
     int64_t d[MSA_WRLEN / 64];
 };
 
+/*
+ * Ingenic MXU2 vector register.  Stored as two host-endian 64-bit halves,
+ * d[0] holding bytes 0..7 of the little-endian memory image (what LU1Q
+ * loads); the narrower views are accessed through the MXU2_H* macros of
+ * mxu2_helper.c / mxu2_translate.c so element n is the same on any host.
+ */
+typedef union MXU2Reg {
+    uint64_t d[2];
+    uint32_t w[4];
+    uint16_t h[8];
+    uint8_t  b[16];
+} MXU2Reg;
+
 typedef union fpr_t fpr_t;
 union fpr_t {
     float64  fd;   /* ieee double precision */
@@ -1103,7 +1116,7 @@ typedef struct CPUArchState {
 #define EXCP_INST_NOTAVAIL 0x2 /* No valid instruction word for BadInstr */
     uint32_t hflags;    /* CPU State */
     /* TMASK defines different execution modes */
-#define MIPS_HFLAG_TMASK  0x3F5807FF
+#define MIPS_HFLAG_TMASK  0x7F5807FF
 #define MIPS_HFLAG_MODE   0x00007 /* execution modes                    */
     /*
      * The KSU flags must be the lowest bits in hflags. The flag order
@@ -1161,6 +1174,7 @@ typedef struct CPUArchState {
 #define MIPS_HFLAG_ELPA  0x4000000
 #define MIPS_HFLAG_ITC_CACHE  0x8000000 /* CACHE instr. operates on ITC tag */
 #define MIPS_HFLAG_ERL   0x10000000 /* error level flag */
+#define MIPS_HFLAG_CU2   0x40000000 /* Status.CU2 on a CPU with MXU2 */
     target_ulong btarget;        /* Jump / branch target               */
     target_ulong bcond;          /* Branch condition (if needed)       */
 
@@ -1170,6 +1184,12 @@ typedef struct CPUArchState {
     uint32_t CP0_TCStatus_rw_bitmask; /* Read/write bits in CP0_TCStatus */
     uint64_t insn_flags; /* Supported instruction set */
 
+    /* Ingenic MXU2 (ASE_MXU2): 32 x 128-bit registers and MCSR ($31) */
+    struct {
+        MXU2Reg vr[32] QEMU_ALIGNED(16);
+        uint32_t mcsr;
+    } mxu2;
+
     /* Fields up to this point are cleared by a CPU reset */
     struct {} end_reset_fields;
 
